<title>JAPAN: Japan Jan-March stainless steel demand seen down.</title>
<headline>Japan Jan-March stainless steel demand seen down.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1996-12-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Japan's domestic demand for stainless steel is expected to fall 3.4 percent in the January-March quarter next year compared with the same period of this year to 181,500 tonnes per month, the Ministry of International Trade and Industry said on Thursday.</p>
<p>In its quarterly outlook for special steel demand, the ministry also predicted exports would rise 9.1 percent year on year to 80,200 tonnes per month during the quarter.</p>
<p>--Tokyo Commodity Desk +81-3-3432-6179</p>
</text>
